# Experiment F: failure and recovery on tier S data (one poison message, one duplicate, 50 normal
# messages on the embedding queue). Phase 15 Wave 2.
# UNAPPROVED and UNEXECUTED. Format: scripts/README.md, "Experiment manifest contract".
# No spaces in values.
# PLACEHOLDERS the human replaces before an approval record is written
# (the record binds the sha256 of the final file, so any edit needs a new record):
#   ACCOUNT_ID       123456789012 is the documented example, not a real account.
#   (DATASET_SNAPSHOT is filled: scholarchain-s-20261107-10dd7f34121b, reported by WO-4 and
#                    verified by the human.)
#   OUTPUT_ROOT      /abs/outside/repo/... is a placeholder path; pick a durable directory
#                    outside the repository.
# The entry point injects exactly one fault kind (a poison message, schemaVersion 2) plus one
# duplicate delivery, handles it and exits 0 when recovery is shown (derive_f.py judges afterwards).
# Under first-failure a nonzero exit ends the run as FAILED with no retry, and the failed record is
# kept, never discarded.
# Limits (tier S caps of decision P15-1: 90 min, 64 clients, 20000 tasks):
#   MAX_TASKS 200    messages including the fault; the run sends 52 (50 normal, 1 poison, 1 duplicate)
#                    and the entry point refuses less than 52.
#   MAX_MINUTES 30   the poll runs MAX_MINUTES minus 5 = 25 min. The poison message needs 3
#                    receives, each followed by a visibility timeout: about 6 min at the worker's
#                    120 s, about 15 min at the queue default 300 s. Both fit in 25 min. If WO-10 sets
#                    a longer visibility timeout, raise MAX_MINUTES (ceiling check: 40 min is 0.27 USD
#                    at the burn below, over the 0.25 ceiling, so the ceiling must rise too) and
#                    regenerate.
# COST (HOURLY_BURN_USD and SPEND_CEILING_USD): session 2 values from WO-10, infra/terraform/COST_ESTIMATE.md,
# section "Session 2 (services) hourly burn and HIGH", paragraph "Provisional experiment burns".
# HOURLY_BURN_USD 0.40 = the steady burn 0.37 rounded up (no extra tasks). Was 0.62 (tier M draft).
# SPEND_CEILING_USD 0.25: 0.40 x 30 min / 60 = 0.20, under the ceiling 0.25 (0.05 headroom). Was 0.50.
# The burn covers the experiment hours only.
# CAVEAT for the human: every rate behind the 0.37 steady burn is UNVERIFIED (memory; only the
# Fargate per-second rates are read anchors), so the value is the WO-10 figure, not a verified rate.
MANIFEST_VERSION=1
EXPERIMENT_ID=F
DESCRIPTION=failure-and-recovery-retry-dead-letter-idempotency-tier-s
ENVIRONMENT=course
REGION=us-east-2
ACCOUNT_ID=123456789012
DATASET_SNAPSHOT=scholarchain-s-20261107-10dd7f34121b
SIZE_TIER=S
MAX_MINUTES=30
MAX_CONCURRENCY=2
MAX_TASKS=200
SPEND_CEILING_USD=0.25
HOURLY_BURN_USD=0.40
STOP_CONDITIONS=wall-clock,first-failure,spend-estimate
METRIC_NAMES=ApproximateNumberOfMessagesVisible,ApproximateNumberOfMessagesNotVisible,ApproximateAgeOfOldestMessage,NumberOfMessagesSent,NumberOfMessagesReceived,NumberOfMessagesDeleted,DesiredTaskCount,RunningTaskCount,CPUUtilization,MemoryUtilization
METRIC_NAMESPACES=AWS/SQS,ECS/ContainerInsights,AWS/ECS
OUTPUT_ROOT=/abs/outside/repo/scholarchain-experiments
ENTRY_POINT=script:experiments/f-failure-recovery/run.sh
